  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The wall pass – round the cone and cut in",
  "description": "One line a little way out from one corner and a few passers in the corner. A passes to the passers in the corner, skates down and around the cone by the board and gets the puck back. Then A passes to B, who is now first in the line, and gets it straight back. A curves in towards goal with the puck and shoots.\n\nThe drill is mainly about passing but also works as a warm-up with a finish. Change the passers now and then. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass on the move – do not stop to receive."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The wall passes should be first time."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Curve in towards goal so you get a good shooting angle."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 2,
